# Kim et al. (2020, ApJ 904, 111), Table 5 ("Binned QLFs"), Case 1 columns; checked against arXiv:2010.05859v1
# Sample: IMS z ~ 5 quasars; Case 1 = broad-band colour selection only (43 quasars), which the paper adopts as its representative result.
#         (Case 2 = broad-band + medium-band selection, 32-quasar subset; same sample, not independent of Case 1.)
# Redshift: 4.7 < z < 5.4
# Magnitude definition: M1450; bin width 0.5 mag
# Phi convention: linear Phi in units of 1e-9 cMpc^-3 mag^-1 (H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7); errors are root-sum-square 1/Va errors
# Note: The faintest Case 1 bin (-23.25) is boosted by one serendipitously found quasar in a low-completeness region (IMS J085028-050607);
#       the paper says it is still consistent with its best fit within 1 sigma. Case 2 gives 68.1 +- 39.3 there.
# Note: The re-binned Yang et al. (2016) bright points (M1450 < -27) in Table 5 are excluded; Yang et al. (2016) is a separate entry.
#
# M1450  Phi  Delta
 -27.250  4.7  4.7
 -26.750  4.7  4.7
 -26.250  15.1  8.7
 -25.750  16.5  9.5
 -25.250  30.8  13.8
 -24.750  48.1  18.2
 -24.250  70.7  22.4
 -23.750  59.0  22.3
 -23.250  104.1  42.5
